==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈmaʊ̯ər/|[ˈmaʊ̯.ɐ]}}
* {{rhymes|de|aʊ̯ɐ|s=2}}
* {{audio|de|De-Mauer.ogg|Audio}}

===Etymology 1===
{{dercat|de|la}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|mūr, mūre}}, from {{inh|de|goh|mūra}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*mūrā|t=wall}}. Cognate with {{cog|yi|מויער}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|f|dim=^chen,^lein}}

# a [[wall]], usually one made of [[stone]] or [[concrete]]
# {{lb|de|figurative|sports}} several [[player]]s forming a [[blockade]] against the [[ball]]

=====Usage notes=====
* See {{m|de|Wand}} for notes on the distinction between ''Mauer'' and this sometimes interchangeable word.

